    <oops:hasDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This pitfall consists in missing the definition of equivalent classes (owl:equivalentClass) in case of duplicated concepts. When an ontology reuses terms from other ontologies, classes that have the same meaning should be defined as equivalent in order to benefit the interoperability between both ontologies.	</oops:hasDescription>
